---
import Analytics from '../../components/Analytics.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import ShareBar from '../../components/ShareBar.astro';
import SiteSearch from '../../components/SiteSearch.astro';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <Analytics />
  <title>The Three Angels' Messages — Revelation 14 &amp; 18</title>
  <meta name="description" content="The Three Angels' Messages of Revelation 14:6–12 and the joining angel of Revelation 18:1–5. The final test for eternity. Come out of Babylon." />
  <meta property="og:title" content="The Three Angels' Messages — Revelation 14 &amp; 18">
  <meta property="og:description" content="The Three Angels' Messages of Revelation 14:6–12 and the joining angel of Revelation 18:1–5. The final test for eternity. Come out of Babylon.">
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://sundaylaw.com/images/shield_sundaylaw.com_the_final_warning_logo.jpg">
  <meta property="og:type" content="article">
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://sundaylaw.com/books/3angels">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:wght@500;600;700&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #060814;
      --ink: #f4f0df;
      --muted: #c5bb95;
      --line: rgba(212,165,55,0.26);
      --gold: #d4a537;
      --amber: #f0cf7b;
    }
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    body {
      font-family: 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif;
      color: var(--ink);
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 76% 14%, rgba(212,165,55,0.16), transparent 36%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 16% 80%, rgba(75,105,170,0.18), transparent 44%),
        linear-gradient(160deg, #05060f 0%, #0a0d1b 52%, #070910 100%);
      overflow-x: hidden;
    }
    .serif { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; }

    /* NAV */
    .topbar { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 30; backdrop-filter: blur(10px); background: rgba(6,8,20,0.76); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .topbar-inner { max-width: 1160px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 14px 22px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 14px; }
    .brand { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .brand strong { color: var(--amber); }
    .toplinks { display: flex; gap: 14px; }
    .toplinks a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .toplinks a:hover { color: var(--amber); }

    /* HERO */
    .hero { max-width: 1000px; margin: 48px auto 0; padding: 0 22px; }
    .hero-card { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 24px; padding: 44px 36px; background: linear-gradient(150deg, rgba(16,24,45,0.95), rgba(8,12,24,0.9)); box-shadow: 0 22px 66px rgba(0,0,0,0.46); }
    .eyebrow { display: inline-block; padding: 7px 14px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--amber); letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.74rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; }
    .hero-card h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5.5vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.05; margin: 0; }
    .hero-card h1 span { color: var(--amber); }
    .hero-card .lead { margin: 16px 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8; max-width: 72ch; }

    /* LAYOUT */
    .layout { max-width: 1000px; margin: 28px auto 80px; padding: 0 22px; display: grid; gap: 18px; }

    /* ANGEL SECTION */
    .angel { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 20px; background: rgba(13,19,36,0.88); overflow: hidden; }
    .angel-header { padding: 20px 26px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; }
    .angel-num { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 44px; height: 44px; border-radius: 50%; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 800; flex-shrink: 0; }
    .num-1 { background: rgba(212,165,55,0.18); border: 1.5px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.5); color: var(--amber); }
    .num-2 { background: rgba(100,160,212,0.16); border: 1.5px solid rgba(100,160,212,0.4); color: #93c5fd; }
    .num-3 { background: rgba(220,80,60,0.14); border: 1.5px solid rgba(220,80,60,0.38); color: #f87171; }
    .num-4 { background: rgba(140,100,220,0.14); border: 1.5px solid rgba(140,100,220,0.38); color: #c4b5fd; }
    .angel-header h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 0; }
    .angel-header .ref { color: var(--amber); font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
    .angel-body { padding: 24px 26px; }

    /* SCRIPTURE QUOTE */
    .scripture { border-left: 4px solid var(--gold); background: rgba(212,165,55,0.07); border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0; padding: 18px 20px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
    .scripture p { font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.82; color: #fef3c7; font-style: italic; margin: 0; }
    .scripture cite { display: block; margin-top: 10px; color: var(--amber); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.88rem; font-style: normal; }

    /* EGW QUOTE */
    .egw { position: relative; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a0f0a, #0d0a06); border: 1px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.32); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 22px 18px 44px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
    .egw::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 20px; top: 18px; bottom: 18px; width: 3px; background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #d97706, #92400e); border-radius: 2px; }
    .egw p { color: rgba(254,243,199,0.9); font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.78; font-style: italic; margin: 0; }
    .egw cite { display: block; margin-top: 10px; color: #d97706; font-size: 0.87rem; font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; }

    /* BODY TEXT */
    .angel-body p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.82; margin-bottom: 14px; }
    .angel-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .angel-body strong { color: var(--ink); }

    /* CALL OUT BOX */
    .callout { border: 1px solid rgba(220,80,60,0.38); border-radius: 14px; background: rgba(220,80,60,0.07); padding: 20px 22px; margin-top: 14px; }
    .callout h4 { margin: 0 0 10px; color: #f87171; font-size: 1.1rem; }
    .callout p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.8; margin: 0; }
    .callout p + p { margin-top: 10px; }

    /* CHART SECTION */
    .chart-section { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 20px; background: rgba(13,19,36,0.88); padding: 28px; }
    .chart-section h2 { margin: 0 0 16px; color: var(--amber); font-size: 1.7rem; }
    .chart-img { width: 100%; max-width: 860px; display: block; margin: 0 auto 18px; border-radius: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--line); box-shadow: 0 18px 50px rgba(0,0,0,0.5); }
    .chart-btns { display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 22px; justify-content: center; }
    .chart-btns a { padding: 10px 20px; border-radius: 10px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.9rem; text-decoration: none; transition: all 0.2s; }
    .btn-gold { background: var(--gold); color: #111; }
    .btn-gold:hover { background: var(--amber); }
    .btn-outline { border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); }
    .btn-outline:hover { border-color: rgba(212,165,55,0.5); color: var(--amber); }
    .pdf-embed { width: 100%; height: 680px; border: 1px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.22); border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; display: block; }

    /* PDF SOURCE */
    .source-section { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 20px; background: rgba(13,19,36,0.88); padding: 28px; }
    .source-section h2 { margin: 0 0 14px; color: var(--amber); font-size: 1.5rem; }
    .source-section p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 14px; }
    .source-links { display: grid; gap: 8px; margin-top: 14px; }
    .source-links a { color: var(--amber); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
    .source-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

    /* FOOTER */
    footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); background: rgba(8,10,20,0.7); padding: 18px 22px; text-align: center; color: #8c8f9f; font-size: 0.88rem; margin-top: 40px; }
    footer a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; margin: 0 10px; }
    footer a:hover { color: var(--amber); }

    @media (max-width: 680px) {
      .hero-card { padding: 28px 20px; }
      .angel-body { padding: 18px; }
      .angel-header { padding: 16px 18px 14px; }
      .pdf-embed { height: 480px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="topbar-inner">
      <a class="brand" href="/">Advent <strong>Pioneer Library</strong></a>
      <nav class="toplinks" aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="/pioneers">Pioneers</a>
        <a href="/books">Books</a>
        <a href="/prophecy-charts">Prophecy Charts</a>
        <a href="/prophecy-explained">Prophecy Study</a>
        <a href="/april-15-1904-new-organization">1904 Record</a>
        <a href="/midnight-cry">1844 Midnight Cry Movie</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>

    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-card">
        <span class="eyebrow">Revelation 14:6–12 &amp; 18:1–5</span>
        <h1 class="serif">The Three Angels' <span>Messages</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">
          The everlasting gospel proclaimed to every nation, kindred, tongue, and people.
          The final warning before the close of probation. The seal of God versus the mark of the beast.
          The last test for eternity — determined by whether you come out of Babylon.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="layout">

      <!-- ===== FIRST ANGEL ===== -->
      <article class="angel">
        <div class="angel-header">
          <span class="angel-num num-1 serif">I</span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="serif">The First Angel's Message</h2>
            <span class="ref">Revelation 14:6–7 · c. 1840–1844</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="angel-body">
          <div class="scripture">
            <p>"And I saw another angel fly in the midst of heaven, having the everlasting gospel to preach unto them
            that dwell on the earth, and to every nation, and kindred, and tongue, and people, saying with a loud voice,
            Fear God, and give glory to him; for the hour of his judgment is come: and worship him that made heaven,
            and earth, and the sea, and the fountains of waters."</p>
            <cite>— Revelation 14:6–7 (KJV)</cite>
          </div>
          <p>
            The First Angel calls all the world back to the <strong>Creator God</strong> — the God who <em>made</em> heaven and earth,
            the sea and the fountains of waters. This is a direct reference to the fourth commandment (Exodus 20:8–11),
            the Sabbath of creation, which identifies the true God from all false systems of worship.
          </p>
          <p>
            The proclamation "the hour of His judgment is come" pointed prophetically to <strong>October 22, 1844</strong> —
            the end of the 2,300-day prophecy of Daniel 8:14, when Christ entered the Most Holy Place of the
            heavenly sanctuary to begin the investigative judgment. William Miller, Charles Fitch, Apollos Hale,
            and a host of Advent preachers carried this message across the United States and the world from
            approximately 1840 to 1844.
          </p>
          <div class="egw">
            <p>"The first angel's message of Revelation 14, announcing the hour of God's judgment and calling upon
            men to fear and worship Him, was designed to separate the professed people of God from the corrupting
            influences of the world and to arouse them to see their true condition of worldliness and backsliding."</p>
            <cite>— Ellen G. White, The Great Controversy, p. 379</cite>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- ===== SECOND ANGEL ===== -->
      <article class="angel">
        <div class="angel-header">
          <span class="angel-num num-2 serif">II</span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="serif">The Second Angel's Message</h2>
            <span class="ref">Revelation 14:8 · Summer 1844</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="angel-body">
          <div class="scripture">
            <p>"And there followed another angel, saying, Babylon is fallen, is fallen, that great city,
            because she made all nations drink of the wine of the wrath of her fornication."</p>
            <cite>— Revelation 14:8 (KJV)</cite>
          </div>
          <p>
            In the summer of 1844, Charles Fitch preached his landmark sermon <em>"Come Out of Her, My People"</em>
            — calling all true believers to separate from the fallen Protestant churches that had rejected the
            First Angel's Message. When the churches closed their doors to the Advent message, they fell from
            their position of favor with God. Babylon — confusion — describes any church that mixes human tradition
            with the commandments of God.
          </p>
          <p>
            The <strong>Midnight Cry of Matthew 25:6</strong> — "Behold, the bridegroom cometh; go ye out to meet him" —
            joined and amplified the Second Angel's Message in the autumn of 1844, producing the great
            Seventh-Month Movement. Tens of thousands came out of the established churches in preparation
            for October 22, 1844.
          </p>
          <div class="egw">
            <p>"As the churches refused to receive the first angel's message, they rejected the light from heaven
            and fell from the favor of God. They trusted to their own strength, and by opposing the first message
            placed themselves where they could not see the light of the second angel's message."</p>
            <cite>— Ellen G. White, Early Writings, p. 237</cite>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- ===== THIRD ANGEL ===== -->
      <article class="angel">
        <div class="angel-header">
          <span class="angel-num num-3 serif">III</span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="serif">The Third Angel's Message</h2>
            <span class="ref">Revelation 14:9–12 · From October 22, 1844 onward</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="angel-body">
          <div class="scripture">
            <p>"And the third angel followed them, saying with a loud voice, If any man worship the beast and his image,
            and receive his mark in his forehead, or in his hand, the same shall drink of the wine of the wrath of God,
            which is poured out without mixture into the cup of his indignation; and he shall be tormented with fire and
            brimstone in the presence of the holy angels, and in the presence of the Lamb: And the smoke of their torment
            ascendeth up for ever and ever: and they have no rest day nor night, who worship the beast and his image,
            and whosoever receiveth the mark of his name. Here is the patience of the saints: here are they that
            keep the commandments of God, and the faith of Jesus."</p>
            <cite>— Revelation 14:9–12 (KJV)</cite>
          </div>
          <p>
            The Third Angel's Message is the most solemn warning in Scripture. It warns against worshiping the beast
            and his image — the Papacy and any civil-religious system that enforces false worship — and against
            receiving his mark. The seal of God (the seventh-day Sabbath, Revelation 7; Ezekiel 20:12,20) stands
            in direct opposition to the mark of the beast (Sunday observance enforced by civil law).
          </p>
          <p>
            The people who survive this final test are described plainly: <strong>"they that keep the commandments
            of God, and the faith of Jesus"</strong> (Revelation 14:12). All ten commandments. The seventh-day
            Sabbath included. This is the identifying mark of the 144,000 — those sealed before the close of
            probation (Revelation 7:1–4; Daniel 12:1).
          </p>
          <div class="egw">
            <p>"The third angel's message is to lighten the earth with its glory. How important, then, that we
            stand in the right position to receive this message. Let us not through our own perversity dishonor God,
            and misrepresent the precious truth that has been given us."</p>
            <cite>— Ellen G. White, Testimonies for the Church, Vol. 6, p. 401</cite>
          </div>
          <div class="callout">
            <h4 class="serif">The Final Test — Commandments of God vs. Mark of the Beast</h4>
            <p>
              The Third Angel draws the final line in earth's history. On one side: those who keep
              the <strong>commandments of God and the faith of Jesus</strong> — including the seventh-day Sabbath
              (the fourth commandment, Exodus 20:8–11; the seal of the living God, Revelation 7:2–3).
            </p>
            <p>
              On the other side: those who worship the beast and his image — any church-state union that enforces
              false worship by civil law, mirroring the model of the Papacy, which changed the Sabbath from the
              seventh day to the first day without biblical authority.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- ===== FOURTH ANGEL / REVELATION 18 ===== -->
      <article class="angel">
        <div class="angel-header">
          <span class="angel-num num-4 serif">18</span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="serif">The Angel of Revelation 18 Joins</h2>
            <span class="ref">Revelation 18:1–5 · The Loud Cry</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="angel-body">
          <div class="scripture">
            <p>"And after these things I saw another angel come down from heaven, having great power;
            and the earth was lightened with his glory. And he cried mightily with a strong voice, saying,
            Babylon the great is fallen, is fallen, and is become the habitation of devils, and the hold of
            every foul spirit, and a cage of every unclean and hateful bird. For all nations have drunk of
            the wine of the wrath of her fornication, and the kings of the earth have committed fornication
            with her, and the merchants of the earth are waxed rich through the abundance of her delicacies.
            And I heard another voice from heaven, saying, Come out of her, my people, that ye be not
            partakers of her sins, and that ye receive not of her plagues. For her sins have reached unto
            heaven, and God hath remembered her iniquities."</p>
            <cite>— Revelation 18:1–5 (KJV)</cite>
          </div>
          <p>
            Just as the Midnight Cry (Matthew 25:6) joined and amplified the Second Angel's Message in 1844,
            so the angel of Revelation 18 joins the Third Angel's Message in final power —
            the <strong>Loud Cry</strong>. The message of Babylon's fall is repeated with additional force,
            now including <strong>the corruptions that have been entering the churches since 1844</strong>.
          </p>
          <div class="egw">
            <p>"The message of the fall of Babylon, as given by the second angel, is repeated, with the
            additional mention of the corruptions which have been entering the churches since 1844.
            The work of this angel comes in at the right time to join in the last great work of the
            third angel's message as it swells to a loud cry."</p>
            <cite>— Ellen G. White, Early Writings, p. 277.1</cite>
          </div>
          <div class="egw">
            <p>"This message seemed to be an addition to the third message, joining it as the midnight cry
            joined the second angel's message in 1844… proclaiming the fall of Babylon and calling upon
            God's people to come out of her."</p>
            <cite>— Ellen G. White, Early Writings, p. 277.2</cite>
          </div>
          <div class="egw">
            <p>"When the messages of the three angels come prominently before the world again just before
            the second advent of Christ, the angel of Revelation 18:1 joins in the proclamation of the
            second angel in the message that 'Babylon is fallen.' 'Come out of her, my people.'"</p>
            <cite>— Ellen G. White, Early Writings, Appendix, p. 304.1</cite>
          </div>

          <!-- BABYLON / COME OUT -->
          <div class="callout" style="border-color:rgba(212,165,55,0.4);background:rgba(212,165,55,0.06);">
            <h4 class="serif" style="color:var(--amber);">What Is Babylon? — The Final Test for Eternity</h4>
            <p>
              Babylon means <em>confusion</em>. It describes every religious system that mixes the commandments
              of men with the commandments of God. In the final crisis, Babylon is specifically the
              <strong>church-state union</strong> — any church organization that submits to civil government
              control of religion.
            </p>
            <p>
              The IRS 501(c)(3) tax-exempt status is a legally binding contract between a church and the
              civil government. The historic Adventist pioneers already had what they needed spiritually —
              but by choosing to incorporate under civil law (April 15, 1904) and register with the government,
              the "new organization" joined church and state together, creating an image of the same system
              the Pilgrim fathers fled Europe to escape in 1620.
            </p>
            <p>
              The Pilgrims left England on the Mayflower, landing at Plymouth Rock in 1620, to escape
              the Church of England — a state-controlled church that persecuted those who would not
              conform to its forms of worship. The Vatican's model of joining church and state to
              enforce religious observance is the very system the Book of Revelation calls Babylon.
              <strong>To form another image of that same system on American soil is the fulfillment
              of Revelation 13:11–17.</strong>
            </p>
            <p>
              God's call is plain: <em>"Come out of her, my people, that ye be not partakers of her sins,
              and that ye receive not of her plagues."</em> — Revelation 18:4.
              Come into home churches. Study the original books, tracts, sermons, and prophecy charts
              of the historic Adventist pioneers. Keep the commandments of God. Hold the faith of Jesus.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- ===== TWO GROUPS — TWO FOUNDATIONS ===== -->
      <article class="angel" id="two-foundations">
        <div class="angel-header">
          <span class="angel-num num-4 serif" style="font-size:0.75rem;width:54px;border-radius:12px;">Matt 25</span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="serif">Two Groups — Two Different Foundations</h2>
            <span class="ref">Matthew 25:1–13 · The Wise and Foolish Virgins</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="angel-body">

          <div class="scripture">
            <p>"Then shall the kingdom of heaven be likened unto ten virgins, which took their lamps, and went forth
            to meet the bridegroom. And five of them were wise, and five were foolish. They that were foolish took
            their lamps, and took no oil with them: But the wise took oil in their vessels with their lamps.
            While the bridegroom tarried, they all slumbered and slept. And at midnight there was a cry made,
            Behold, the bridegroom cometh; go ye out to meet him… And they that were ready went in with him
            to the marriage: and the door was shut."</p>
            <cite>— Matthew 25:1–6, 10 (KJV)</cite>
          </div>

          <p>
            The parable of the ten virgins describes the Advent movement exactly.
            All ten went out to meet the Bridegroom. All ten had lamps — a profession of truth.
            But only five had <strong>oil</strong> — the Holy Spirit, living obedience, the commandments of God kept in faith.
            The dividing line was not visible from the outside. It was internal. Foundational.
          </p>

          <div class="grid-2" style="display:grid;gap:18px;margin:20px 0;">

            <!-- WISE VIRGINS -->
            <div style="border:2px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.45);border-radius:16px;padding:22px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(30,24,5,0.75),rgba(10,13,28,0.88));">
              <div style="display:inline-block;padding:4px 12px;border-radius:999px;background:rgba(212,165,55,0.14);border:1px solid rgba(212,165,55,0.4);color:var(--amber);font-size:0.74rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:12px;">The Wise Virgins</div>
              <h3 class="serif" style="color:var(--amber);margin:0 0 12px;font-size:1.3rem;">The Original Foundation</h3>
              <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 10px;line-height:1.8;font-weight:700;">Built on October 22, 1844</p>
              <p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 10px;">
                The historic Adventist pioneers came out of Babylon in response to the Second Angel's cry.
                They laid their foundation on the prophetic waymarks — the heavenly sanctuary, the seventh-day
                Sabbath, the Three Angels' Messages, the commandments of God, and the faith of Jesus.
                They rejected every vestige of Papal tradition.
              </p>
              <ul style="margin:0 0 14px 18px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.9;list-style:disc;">
                <li>Foundation: October 22, 1844 — Daniel 8:14</li>
                <li>Oil: Sabbath, Sanctuary, Seal of God</li>
                <li>Standard: Commandments of God + Faith of Jesus</li>
                <li>Lamp: The Present Truth — James White, 1849</li>
                <li>Cry: Three Angels' Messages — Revelation 14:6–12</li>
                <li>Goal: The 144,000 sealed — Revelation 7; Daniel 12:1</li>
              </ul>
              <a href="/pioneers" style="display:inline-block;padding:9px 18px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--gold);color:#111;font-weight:700;font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">Explore the Historic Pioneers →</a>
            </div>

            <!-- FOOLISH VIRGINS -->
            <div style="border:2px solid rgba(220,60,60,0.38);border-radius:16px;padding:22px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(40,5,5,0.75),rgba(10,13,28,0.88));">
              <div style="display:inline-block;padding:4px 12px;border-radius:999px;background:rgba(220,60,60,0.12);border:1px solid rgba(220,60,60,0.38);color:#f87171;font-size:0.74rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:12px;">The Foolish Virgins</div>
              <h3 class="serif" style="color:#f87171;margin:0 0 12px;font-size:1.3rem;">The New Organization Foundation</h3>
              <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 10px;line-height:1.8;font-weight:700;">Built on April 15, 1904</p>
              <p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 10px;">
                The new organization incorporated on April 15, 1904, creating the
                <em>General Conference Corporation of Seventh-day Adventists</em> under civil law — joining
                church and state together. Lamps but no oil. A profession of truth without the living
                obedience. Roman hierarchical structure. Catholic doctrines brought back in.
                "Another universal and truly Catholic organization." (Review, March 5, 1981)
              </p>
              <ul style="margin:0 0 14px 18px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.9;list-style:disc;">
                <li>Foundation: April 15, 1904 — civil incorporation</li>
                <li>No oil: Church joined to state — EIN 52-0643036</li>
                <li>Standard: Government-registered corporation</li>
                <li>Path: Same as fallen Protestant churches in 1844</li>
                <li>Image: Papacy / Church of England / Vatican model</li>
                <li>End: "The door was shut" — Matthew 25:10</li>
              </ul>
              <a href="/april-15-1904-new-organization" style="display:inline-block;padding:9px 18px;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid rgba(220,60,60,0.4);color:#f87171;font-weight:700;font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">View the 1904 Incorporation Record →</a>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div class="egw">
            <p>"Adventists from 1844 onward built on the everlasting gospel — the commandments of God and
            the faith of Jesus. The new organization of 1904 built on a civil charter. One foundation
            is the Rock. The other is sand. The storm is coming."</p>
            <cite>— Paraphrase from Matthew 7:24–27 applied to the Advent movement</cite>
          </div>

          <div class="callout" style="border-color:rgba(212,165,55,0.4);background:rgba(212,165,55,0.05);">
            <h4 class="serif" style="color:var(--amber);">Ellen White Warned Before It Happened</h4>
            <p>
              "The enemy of souls has sought to bring in the supposition that a great reformation was to take
              place among Seventh-day Adventists, and that this reformation would consist in giving up the
              doctrines which stand as the <strong>pillars of our faith</strong>, and engaging in a process of
              <strong>reorganization</strong>. Were this reformation to take place, what would result?
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top:10px;">
              The principles of truth that God in His wisdom has given to the remnant church, would be discarded.
              Our religion would be changed. The fundamental principles that have sustained the work for the last
              fifty years would be accounted as error. <strong>A new organization would be established.</strong>
              Books of a new order would be written. A system of intellectual philosophy would be introduced."
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top:10px;">
              "We cannot now step off the foundation that God has established. We cannot now enter into
              any new organization; for this would mean apostasy from the truth."
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top:8px;color:#9ca3af;font-size:0.88rem;font-style:italic;">— Ellen G. White, Selected Messages Book 1, p. 204.2</p>
            <p style="margin-top:12px;">
              This warning was given <em>before</em> April 15, 1904. The new organization was formed anyway.
              The wise virgins hear the warning and keep their oil. The foolish hear it — and go in
              without it anyway.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- ===== JAMES WHITE — MESSAGE OF THE 144,000 ===== -->
      <article class="angel" id="message-of-144000">
        <div class="angel-header">
          <span class="angel-num num-1 serif" style="font-size:0.85rem;width:54px;border-radius:12px;">Q&amp;A</span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="serif">What Is the Message of the 144,000?</h2>
            <span class="ref">Answered by Elder James White — "The Modern Moses"</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="angel-body">

          <div class="egw">
            <p>"The third angel's message was, and still is, a WARNING to the saints to 'hold fast,'
            and not go back, and 'receive' THE MARKS which the virgin band got rid of, during the
            second angel's cry."</p>
            <cite>— James White, <em>A Word to the "Little Flock"</em>, April 21, 1847, p. 11</cite>
          </div>

          <p>
            The message of the 144,000 is not a new message — it is the recovery and holding fast of
            every truth the Second Angel's cry exposed and separated God's people from.
            The marks of Babylon that the virgin band <em>got rid of</em> in 1843–1844 must never be
            received again. That is what James White called the Third Angel's Message.
          </p>

          <p>
            Yet in 1856 — only nine years after writing those words — James White warned that the
            movement was already beginning to drift. Elder White, sometimes called the Modern Moses,
            identified four specific dangers the emerging denomination faced:
          </p>

          <div class="callout" style="border-color:rgba(212,165,55,0.38);background:rgba(212,165,55,0.05);">
            <h4 class="serif" style="color:var(--amber);">The Reformers Stopped Reforming</h4>
            <p>
              "The greatest fault we can find in the Reformation is, the Reformers stopped reforming…
              had they left the last vestige of Papacy behind — like the Trinity, Sunday sacredness,
              natural immortality, sprinkling — the church would now be free from her unscriptural errors."
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top:10px;color:#9ca3af;font-size:0.9rem;font-style:italic;">— James White</p>
          </div>

          <p>
            The pioneers did not borrow from Rome. They <strong>rejected</strong> Rome.
            The marks of Babylon — the doctrines listed above — were precisely what the Second Angel's
            cry called God's people to leave behind. To bring them back in is apostasy from the foundation.
          </p>

          <h3 class="serif" style="color:var(--amber);margin:22px 0 14px;font-size:1.3rem;">The SDA Denomination Followed the Same Path</h3>

          <p>
            The Seventh-day Adventist denomination followed the same trajectory as the fallen Protestant
            churches did in 1843–1844 during the Second Angel's cry. Step by step, the marks that were
            cast off were brought back in. The corporate incorporation of April 15, 1904 — creating the
            <em>General Conference Corporation of Seventh-day Adventists</em> under civil law — joined
            church and state together, creating the very image the pioneers had warned against.
          </p>

          <p>
            That new organization became Babylon the moment it was created on <strong>April 15, 1904</strong>,
            as documented in the 1905 Seventh-day Adventist Yearbook. The record is not hidden.
          </p>

          <div class="chart-btns" style="margin:14px 0 18px;">
            <a href="/books/1904-image-of-papacy/seventh-day-adventist-yearbook-1905.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-gold">View 1905 Yearbook — Incorporation Record</a>
            <a href="/april-15-1904-new-organization" class="btn-outline">April 15, 1904 Documentary Evidence</a>
          </div>

          <h3 class="serif" style="color:#f87171;margin:22px 0 14px;font-size:1.3rem;">The Confession of What It Had Become</h3>

          <div class="callout" style="border-color:rgba(220,80,60,0.45);background:rgba(220,80,60,0.07);">
            <h4 class="serif" style="color:#f87171;">"Another Universal and Truly Catholic Organization"</h4>
            <p>
              "There is another universal and truly Catholic organization, the Seventh-day Adventist Church."
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top:10px;color:#9ca3af;font-size:0.9rem;font-style:italic;">
              — Review and Herald, March 5, 1981 (Neal C. Wilson)
            </p>
            <div style="margin-top:14px;display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
              <a href="/books/1904-image-of-papacy/1981.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-gold" style="font-size:0.88rem;padding:8px 16px;">View Original Document (PDF)</a>
              <a href="/books/adventist-history/AdventistReview1981.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-outline" style="font-size:0.88rem;padding:8px 16px;">Adventist Review 1981 (Full Issue)</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            The path is traceable. From "hold fast and do not receive the marks of Babylon back"
            (James White, 1847) — to "we are another truly Catholic organization" (1981).
            That is what happens when a movement stops reforming, incorporates under civil law,
            adopts Roman hierarchical structures, and trades the commandments of God for the
            approval of the kingdoms of this world.
          </p>

          <h3 class="serif" style="color:var(--amber);margin:22px 0 14px;font-size:1.35rem;">The Final Call — Escape While You Can</h3>

          <p>
            The angel of Revelation 18:1–5 joins the Third Angel's Message with final, earth-lightening
            power. This is the Loud Cry. It unmasks the corruptions that have entered since 1844 and
            calls God's people to complete separation. There is no neutral ground.
          </p>

          <div class="scripture" style="border-color:#f87171;background:rgba(220,80,60,0.07);">
            <p>"Come out of her, my people, that ye be not partakers of her sins,
            and that ye receive not of her plagues. For her sins have reached unto heaven,
            and God hath remembered her iniquities."</p>
            <cite>— Revelation 18:4–5 (KJV)</cite>
          </div>

          <div class="egw" style="border-color:rgba(220,80,60,0.35);">
            <p>"Flee from the Laodicean churches like Lot from Sodom!
            Their teachings lead to destruction — DEATH! DEATH!! eternal DEATH!!!
            is on their track."</p>
            <cite>— Joseph Bates (paraphrase of his Laodicean warning, echoing Flee From Laodicea)</cite>
          </div>

          <p>
            Can you join with those who deny God's word? The April 15, 1904 corporate structure
            became Babylon the moment it was created — a state-recognized, federally registered
            corporation that joined church and state together, exactly as the Vatican did,
            exactly as the Church of England did, exactly as every fallen church did before it.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Pilgrims left England in 1620 on the Mayflower to escape that very thing.
            The call has not changed: <em>Come out of her, my people.</em>
          </p>

        </div>
      </article>

